.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them.\n\n- **Settings:** the number of attempts is set by the class attribute `max_attempts = 3`. The base wait is a new `backoff` argument on `__init__` (default 0.5), and it doubles on each retry.\n- **What gets retried:** only an HTTP 503. Any other HTTP error (such as 500) is raised immediately with no retry. Network errors and timeouts are not retried either.\n- **When retries run out:** if the third attempt also gets a 503, that 503 is raised to the caller as before.\n\nI tested it against a real local HTTP server, with the sleep call replaced so the waits could be recorded:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Waits |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | returns the JSON | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | raises the 503 (no fourth request) | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 500 | raises the 500 straight away | none |\n| 200 | returns the JSON | none |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69720, "requests_cache_write": 108411, "requests_cost_usd": 0.588827, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1639, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial20", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 99, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:00.099116+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 20.849, "t_checker_s": 1.879, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_b